{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"c1","type":"claim","text":"Eliminating a contested obligation removes it from dispute permanently; clarifying an obligation leaves it a site of interpretation that tends to reopen in new words. Direction of adjustment matters more than precision of adjustment.","scope":"Households governed by explicit agreement."},{"id":"c2","type":"claim","text":"Between friends, explicit agreements are unenforceable: available sanctions (confrontation, withdrawal) cost the enforcer about as much as the offender, so each agreement adds a claim requiring memory and interpretation without adding a cheap way to settle it. The number of agreements is itself a cost driver.","scope":"Friendship-based households; not an allegation of bad faith."},{"id":"c3","type":"claim","text":"The asker's description carries the signature of the household's de facto manager: it tracks agreements, notices non-performance, initiates conversations. Two opposite readings fit that signature equally — an over-carrying, under-credited coordinator, or an over-manager whose follow-ups generate part of the friction — and the description alone cannot distinguish them.","grounds":"The wording of the task description; consistent with, not established by, it."},{"id":"c4","type":"claim","text":"If the household runs on the unstated default that unclaimed or undone work falls to whoever is most bothered by it, avoidance is rewarded and no agreement system survives, because the record-keeper becomes residual doer. Whether this default operates here is untested."},{"id":"c5","type":"claim","text":"This account rests on the same single-sided description as the input account; the manager hypothesis in particular could be an artifact of which resident wrote in."},{"id":"d1","type":"claim","text":"The two poses yield different observable outcomes: under agreement technology, doer-worded written agreements reduce dispute frequency within weeks; under coordination load and role, disputes migrate (to enforcement, score-keeping, or new topics) without falling in frequency. The asker can run this comparison themselves."},{"id":"r0","type":"claim","text":"Local restatement of the input account's central conjecture, hosted for contrast because that account's commitment records are not exposed: the disputes are driven by underspecification and schedule drift, so doer-worded written agreements and a fortnightly check-in should come first, with one-on-one outreach to the avoiding friend."},{"id":"o1","type":"objection","text":"Explicitness plausibly changes dispute content rather than dispute frequency: if the grievance is about standing and role, doer-worded notes migrate disputes from 'what did we agree' to 'you're keeping score' or to enforcement of the notes.","target":["r0"],"bearing":"Falsifiable: if written notes collapse dispute frequency within a few weeks, this objection fails and the input's ordering is vindicated for this household."},{"id":"o2","type":"objection","text":"A recurring group check-in institutionalizes the conversation the friend is already avoiding and hardens the two-on-one geometry the input account itself suspects; a fixed agenda converts episodic disputes into a standing tribunal.","target":["r0"],"bearing":"Conjectured risk, not a demonstrated defect: a scheduled low-stakes venue may be less aversive than ambush disputes. Weakens if the avoider attends voluntarily and charge declines."},{"id":"u1","type":"use","text":"Run the input account's cheapest unilateral measure first — doer-worded written notes for the asker's own undertakings — as the diagnostic that discriminates between the poses: keep the input's program if dispute frequency falls, move to the load-reduction sequence below if disputes migrate.","depends":["d1"],"mentions":["r0"]},{"id":"p1","type":"commitment","text":"Shrink the coordination surface before clarifying it: one inventory conversation with the other two marking every currently shared obligation keep, clarify or eliminate, then a four-to-six-week trial of eliminating two or three contested obligations (own-food arrangements, fewer shared items, a tool that deletes a task), watching dispute frequency.","action":"Inventory-and-eliminate conversation, then a bounded trial period.","consequence":"Eliminated obligations leave dispute permanently; risk the conversation turns defensive and 'keep' dominates.","depends":["c1","c2"],"scope":"This household, next one to two months."},{"id":"p2","type":"commitment","text":"Where spillover is low, replace task-by-task negotiation with domain ownership: each resident owns at least one zone outright, including standard and timing, and the owner's word settles disputes inside it; negotiation survives only for irreducibly shared spaces.","consequence":"Interpretation disputes inside owned domains collapse; boundary disputes and unequal domains remain. Requires the others' consent, so cannot be started unilaterally.","depends":["c1"],"scope":"Low-spillover zones in this household only."},{"id":"p3","type":"commitment","text":"Test the manager hypothesis with an announced, bounded stop on initiating and following up (about two weeks): say in advance that it is an experiment, then record who steps up, what degrades, and what the others say.","consequence":"Distinguishes dependence-and-underappreciation from friction-generated-by-follow-ups, which demand opposite responses. A silent version reads as a strike, so the announcement is mandatory.","depends":["c3"],"scope":"Askable unilaterally; one bounded period."},{"id":"p4","type":"commitment","text":"Make the unclaimed-task default explicit: within hygiene and safety limits, unclaimed work goes undone, visibly, and the household absorbs the consequence rather than the most-concerned resident absorbing the task.","consequence":"Removes the reward for avoidance and makes degradation informative; must be agreed with the others, not imposed.","depends":["c4"],"scope":"This household, under any system eventually adopted."},{"id":"p5","type":"commitment","text":"For the avoiding friend, change the medium before the message: try an asynchronous claiming channel (a shared list, no face, no meeting) before any one-on-one outreach, falling back to the input account's one-on-one approach only if it produces silent non-participation.","consequence":"Tests whether the aversive object is the conversation format rather than its content; without p4 fixed first, an async channel routes work to the asker by a new path.","depends":["c4"],"scope":"Contact with the avoiding friend specifically."},{"id":"q1","type":"problem","text":"Which reading of the manager signature holds — exploited coordinator or over-manager — cannot be settled from the asker's side of the description; it needs the bounded stop-test plus the other two residents' own accounts of the problem.","depends":["c3"]},{"id":"q2","type":"problem","text":"How to announce the stop-initiating test so it is not heard as a strike or retaliation is unresolved; the framing carries most of the experiment's risk.","depends":["p3"]},{"id":"q3","type":"problem","text":"How much of this household's coordination is actually reducible is unknown until the inventory conversation happens; kitchen-type spaces may cap the shrink-the-surface route.","depends":["p1"]}],"uptake":["u1","p1","p2","p3","p4","p5"]}